      ],
      "source": "https://www.brisbane.qld.gov.au/events-arts-and-culture/art-and-culture/heritage-trails/fortitude-valley-heritage-trail",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "All Hallows’ Convent, founded by the Sisters of Mercy in 1863, was one of the earliest girls’ schools in Fortitude Valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.brisbane.qld.gov.au/events-arts-and-culture/art-and-culture/heritage-trails/fortitude-valley-heritage-trail",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Before European settlement, the area now known as Fortitude Valley was home to the Meanjin peoples of the Turrbal and Jagera/Yuggera groups.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
